  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "a37017531ab8989cf7642468d0cfb83cf6e1e15e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1530726075,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I couldn't find decent documentation for the \"User Logging\" opcode, so I used the source code of the BlueZ and the Linux kernel from where this protocol originated.\n* Validation of logging frame in Linux kernel:\n  https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/4942fed84b98cfb71d3cdff1a3df0072a57bbdfa/net/bluetooth/hci_sock.c#L1685\n* Log levels comes from Linux kernel:\n  https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/6f0edbb833ec16ab2042073af4846152b455104d/include/linux/kern_levels.h#L30\n* How such frame is created in BlueZ:\n  https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/bluetooth/bluez.git/tree/src/shared/log.c?h=5.69#n47",
          "author": {
            "id": 15621967,
            "username": "doki-nordic",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Dominik Kilian",
